# Keep the build context small and the image reproducible.
#
# The build context is the whole repository, so anything listed here never
# reaches the daemon. Two rules make the difference between a working and a
# failing build:
#
#   1. Never exclude a file a Dockerfile COPYs. A COPY of a path that the
#      ignore rules removed fails the build outright, it does not copy an empty
#      file. package-lock.json must stay: both images run `npm ci`, which refuses
#      to resolve without it and would otherwise install whatever versions the
#      registry serves that day.
#   2. Never ship local state or secrets into an image.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Version control and editor state
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.git/
.gitignore
.claude/
.husky/
.idea/
.vscode/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Node
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# node_modules is reinstalled by `npm ci` and would only invalidate the cache.
# dist is rebuilt by `npm run build`.
node_modules/
dist/
**/node_modules/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
services/ocr/.venv
services/ocr/venv
services/ocr/.cache
services/ocr/output
services/ocr/.ruff_cache
services/ocr/.mypy_cache
services/ocr/.pytest_cache
services/ocr/*.egg-info
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Runtime state, logs and secrets
#
# .env is how the developer configures a local machine. Deployments inject the
# same values as environment variables, and baking a file with a database
# password into an image layer would be a leak that outlives the container.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*.local
**/.env
**/.env.local

storage/
data/
uploads/
*.log
